# Harness backups of production source.
#
# `scripts/dbharness/prove.sh` writes `<file>.orig` beside a file before it
# plants a defect in it, and removes it on the way out. A run that dies in
# between leaves a byte-identical copy of a migration sitting in
# `supabase/migrations/`, where anything that globs the directory may pick it
# up, and where a careless `git add -A` would commit it. Belt and braces: the
# harness deletes the backup on success and refuses to start when it finds a
# stale one, and these patterns stop a survivor being committed regardless.
*.orig
*.bak

# Agent worktrees. `isolation: "worktree"` places an agent's checkout at
# `.claude/worktrees/<agent>/`, INSIDE this repository, and it is a complete
# second copy of SquadLogic -- 376 MB when this entry was written. Untracked
# and unignored, it sat one `git add -A` away from being committed. The same
# belt-and-braces reasoning as the `*.orig` entry above: the harness cleans
# these up, and this stops a survivor being committed when it does not.
.claude/
